# File: tests/blender/test_twist_seams.py
# Generated from: specs/243-detect-and-repair-one-edge-twist-seams-so-geometry-normals-settles/requirements.md
Feature: Twist seams are repaired by cleanup and named by the validator

  @SCN001 @regression
  Scenario: Cleanup repairs a twist seam with a minimal deletion
    Given a closed Klein bottle with a 3-edge tube whose twist seam has 5 edges
    When clean_mesh runs on it
    Then only the 6 faces at the twist seam edges are deleted
    And geometry_findings reports neither geometry.normals nor geometry.twist_seam

  @SCN002 @regression
  Scenario: The repaired mesh is stable
    Given the twist-seam mesh after clean_mesh
    When clean_mesh and geometry_findings run on it three more times
    Then the geometry does not change and no finding appears

  @SCN003 @regression
  Scenario: The validator names the seam
    Given the uncleaned twist-seam mesh
    When geometry_findings runs on it
    Then it reports geometry.twist_seam with 5 seam edges
    And every sample sits at a seam edge midpoint
    And no geometry.normals finding is reported

  @SCN004 @regression
  Scenario: The repair is deterministic
    Given two identical copies of the twist-seam mesh
    When clean_mesh runs on each copy
    Then both copies have identical vertices, faces, and normals

  @SCN005
  Scenario: Meshes without a twist seam are unaffected
    Given the clean crate, a correctly facing open quad, and an inside-out cube
    When clean_mesh and geometry_findings run on them
    Then twist repair deletes no faces and no geometry.twist_seam finding appears
    And their other findings are unchanged

  @SCN006 @regression
  Scenario: Cleanup reports the twist repair
    Given asset "Twist" holding the twist-seam mesh and the clean crate asset
    When cleanup_desktop runs on each
    Then "Twist" reports twist_repair with 6 faces, 5 edges, and seam midpoint samples
    And the crate reports twist_repair with 0 faces, 0 edges, and no samples
